abstract: "A library of subjectivity: the notes of The Subject of Arithmetic, which reads Gödel's theorem a second way, as the boundary of what a subject can refer to, and the books of mathematics, arithmetic, neuroscience, philosophy and physics beside them, published as they are bound."
keywords:
